# Views and Bootstrap

- **Bootstrap 5.3.3**, compiled from Sass by cssbundling-rails
  (`app/assets/stylesheets/application.bootstrap.scss` → `app/assets/builds/application.css`).
  Use Bootstrap utility classes and components; avoid custom CSS when a utility exists.
- **Color mode:** `$color-mode-type: media-query` — the app follows the OS light/dark
  preference. There is no `data-bs-theme` attribute and no theme toggle. Never hardcode a
  color that only reads correctly in one mode; use Bootstrap CSS variables (`var(--bs-body-bg)`,
  `var(--bs-secondary-color)`, `text-body`, `text-secondary`) so both modes work.
- **Custom classes** live in `app/assets/stylesheets/refresh.scss` — keep it small and
  additive. See `ui.mdc` for the class inventory and the design rules.
- **Icons:** Use `bootstrap-icons` font classes (e.g. `<i class="bi bi-pencil"></i>`)
- **Layout:** `app/views/layouts/application.html.erb` with a shared navbar/footer/flash under
  `app/views/shared/`; views use the grid system (`container`, `row`, `col-*`)
- **Flash messages:** styled via the `bootstrap_class_for` helper in `ApplicationHelper`
- **Pagination:** use Pagy's Bootstrap nav helper
- **Charts:** Chartkick helpers, with series assembled in a presenter (`JobTelemetryCharts`),
  not in the template

## Component Patterns

- Modals: `bootstrap.Modal` JS API driven from Stimulus controllers
  (`app/javascript/controllers/`)
- Tabs / tooltips: `bootstrap.Tab`, `bootstrap.Tooltip`
- Forms: Bootstrap form classes (`form-control`, `form-label`, `form-select`, `form-check`)
- Live printer state arrives as Turbo Stream broadcasts from `PrinterLiveBroadcaster`, which
  re-renders `printers/_live_panel` and `printers/_prusalink_status_dot` into targets named by
  `dom_id(printer, :live)` and `dom_id(printer, :prusalink_status)`. If you rename those
  partials or targets, update the broadcaster too — the pairing is not checked at boot.

## ERB Conventions

- Use partials for repeated UI elements; prefix with an underscore
- Prefer `link_to` and `button_to` helpers over raw `<a>` and `<form>` tags
- Use Turbo Frames and Turbo Streams for dynamic updates instead of custom JS
- Keep view logic in helpers (`app/helpers/`) or presenters (`app/services/*_presenter.rb`),
  not in templates
- Gate content on the authorization helpers exposed by `ApplicationController` —
  `logged_in?`, `admin?`, `internal_network?`, `can_clear_prints?` — rather than re-deriving
  permission checks in the view. Hiding a control in the view is not authorization; the
  controller must also enforce it.
